afk: make the task tool's `isolated` flag required whenever isolation is
enabled.

Motivation: upstream treats `isolated` as opt-in-and-optional — a spawn
that omits it silently runs the subagent directly in the parent
worktree (structured-subagent.ts: `isolation?.requested === true`).
Skill text describing the distribution's isolated-parallel workflow in
the indicative mood ("file-editing dispatches run isolated") led models
to believe isolation was the harness default, so implementer subagents
were dispatched without the flag and edited the shared tree. Making the
field required in the isolation-enabled wire schemas forces an explicit
choice on every dispatch; a forgotten flag becomes a schema error the
model self-corrects (the error carries the schema) instead of a silent
in-tree run.

Scope: wire schemas only (types.ts: exported flat `taskSchema`, batch
item schema, and both isolation-enabled `createTaskSchema` variants).
The `TaskItem`/`TaskParams` interfaces stay optional — args stream in
partially during rendering, and internal callers / stale transcripts
bypass arktype (index.ts execute() tolerates unvalidated input). The
eval `agent()` bridge (eval/agent-bridge.ts) keeps its own optional
`isolated` — a deliberate, documented gap: afk's skills route all
dispatching through the task tool, and one-off read-only `agent()`
calls stay ergonomic.

What must survive a rebase:
- The isolation-enabled schemas (flat + batch item) declare `isolated`
  as REQUIRED; the no-isolation / plan-mode schemas keep NOT exposing
  the field at all.
- The tool description (src/prompts/tools/task.md) states: REQUIRED,
  true = snapshot + parked changes, false = edits the parent worktree
  directly, file-editing work MUST be true.
- Tests: wire-schema.test.ts rejects a missing `isolated` on the
  isolation-enabled schema; task-batch.test.ts asserts `required`
  contains "isolated" in batch-item and flat wire schemas and not when
  isolation is off.

Rebased 18.2.10 -> 18.6.0: upstream rewrote the tool description into
a terse form and added a required solutionSpace; `isolated` is required
in the same four isolation-enabled schemas. New in 18.6.0: TaskTool sets
lenientArgValidation, so arktype failures are forwarded raw to execute()
and a missing `isolated` would no longer be a schema error the model
sees. The patch therefore also rejects it at dispatch (planSpawns ->
validateSpawnParams -> missingIsolatedReason) whenever the schema exposes
isolation (#isIsolationExposed: isolation on, plan mode off; shared with
the parameters/description getters) — this dispatch check must survive
future rebases too. The only internal TaskTool.execute caller
(commit/agentic analyze-file) now passes isolated: false explicitly, so
the "internal callers stay optional" scope note above no longer holds for
execute(). Description-wording assertions were dropped from
task-batch.test.ts; a new agent-loop test proves the lenient path rejects
a call without `isolated`; failed-child-artifact.test.ts fixtures gained
explicit isolated: false.

